# Cloudflare Pages custom headers.
#
# JS/CSS get a short-lived cache with forced revalidation -- Pages' default
# (Cache-Control: public, max-age=14400) meant the CDN edge would happily
# keep serving an old cached pro-wallet.js/aadhaar-qr-scan.js/style.css for
# up to 4 hours after a deploy, even though the new version was already
# live at origin. Confirmed directly: cf-cache-status: HIT on the plain
# URL serving stale content, while a cache-busted request to the same URL
# got the new deploy immediately -- the deploy itself was never the
# problem, the edge cache was. `no-cache` still lets the CDN/browser cache
# the response, but forces a revalidation (conditional request against the
# ETag Pages already sets) before ever serving it, so a real code change
# shows up on the next request instead of silently waiting out the cache.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
